WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.270
- How are you?
- Very well.

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:03.590
Thank you very much.
- Oh my god, oh,

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:05.253
the accent, so you're not from here?

00:00:05.253 --> 00:00:06.807
- Sadly not.
- No, where are you from?

00:00:06.807 --> 00:00:08.570
- No, I'm from Wales.

00:00:08.570 --> 00:00:09.403
- Wales?
- Yes.

00:00:09.403 --> 00:00:10.880
- Beautiful, I've played there.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:11.819
- Have you?
- I love Wales, yeah.

00:00:11.819 --> 00:00:12.652
- In Cardiff?
- Yeah.

00:00:12.652 --> 00:00:13.810
- Oh.
- Yeah, I love it there.

00:00:13.810 --> 00:00:14.687
- I hope they were nice to you.

00:00:14.687 --> 00:00:15.520
- They're great.
- Good.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:18.180
- I love going all around
the UK, Europe, I love it.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.070
- Good.
- Yeah.

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:20.410
So, wait, since you're from Wales,

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:22.160
did you grow up watching Mr. Rogers?

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.180
- No, no, very sadly and
all the poorer for it,

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:28.690
sadly he never made it
across the Atlantic so

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:31.040
we never got to know Mr. Rogers.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.510
I have, obviously, in the last few years.

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:35.024
- Yeah.
- And as a result,

00:00:35.024 --> 00:00:37.770
my three-year-old son has, incredibly so.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.592
But no, we were deprived--

00:00:39.592 --> 00:00:40.793
- I have a three-year-old son as well.

00:00:40.793 --> 00:00:41.626
- Aw.
- Yes.

00:00:41.626 --> 00:00:43.057
It's a fun age, sometimes not.
- Yes.

00:00:43.057 --> 00:00:45.365
- Sometimes it's threenager.
- True.

00:00:45.365 --> 00:00:46.198
- Yeah.
- True.

00:00:46.198 --> 00:00:48.540
- So when did you learn about Mr. Rogers?

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:51.770
- Literally when the script
landed in my lap and I

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:56.410
turned to my better half and
I said, "Who's Mr. Rogers?"

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.040
And she went...
(gasping)

00:00:58.040 --> 00:00:59.555
- Oh.
- Get out!

00:00:59.555 --> 00:01:02.130
(audience laughing)
And she very quickly explained

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:05.850
that Mr. Rogers, I was already
familiar with Mr. Rogers,

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:07.730
unbeknown to me because our three year old

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:09.890
was watching Daniel Tiger's Neighborhood.

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:11.500
- Yeah, yes.
- The legacy.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.970
So then I went on to
watch the show on YouTube

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:16.570
and familiarize myself that way.

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:19.700
And Sam, our three year
old, then became transfixed.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:21.090
- Isn't it funny, as a parent,

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:24.040
you're kinda like woo, this is slow!

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:26.100
But then for kid's it's like so important.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.920
- Yes, I quickly realized, initially going

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.280
what's happening, why, has
he forgotten the words,

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:32.681
why is it so slow?
- Yeah.

00:01:32.681 --> 00:01:33.870
(laughing)
- Why is he not,

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:35.910
why are they not cutting, do
they only have one camera?

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:37.471
Why are they not cutting to anything else?

00:01:37.471 --> 00:01:38.304
(laughing)

00:01:38.304 --> 00:01:41.440
And I realized that he
had thought meticulously

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:45.100
about the pacing children
need of a certain age

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:47.080
so that they have the chance to listen

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:49.610
and to process and to feel listened.

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:52.210
This time when he was
being incredibly brave

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:54.470
when he said, you know,
children's entertainment

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:57.140
is becoming about custard pies.

00:01:57.140 --> 00:02:00.350
You need to go the opposite
direction, slow down for them.

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:03.140
- Yeah, and he tackled
subjects that you're afraid

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:04.733
to talk to with your kids, you know?

00:02:04.733 --> 00:02:06.730
- He was so brave.
- Yeah, so brave.

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:08.340
- In every sense.
- Yeah.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.407
But he didn't see it as
brave, that's the cool thing.

00:02:10.407 --> 00:02:11.640
- No, no, he just saw it as something

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:12.797
you should absolutely do.
- Yeah.

00:02:12.797 --> 00:02:15.120
- I'm so happy you're honoring him today,

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:16.420
I think it's so important.

00:02:16.420 --> 00:02:19.110
- I grew up on him so I love Mr. Rogers.

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:22.377
But a big moment is when
Mr. Rogers reminds Lloyd,

00:02:22.377 --> 00:02:24.280
your character in the
movie, he reminds you

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:26.890
of your favorite childhood
toy, Old Rabbit, right?

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:27.850
- Yeah.
- Yeah,

00:02:27.850 --> 00:02:30.240
and that's a really kind of
pivotal moment in the movie?

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:31.590
- Yes, incredibly so.

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:34.263
And I don't know for those
who do know, don't know,

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:37.840
the film is based on this
actual Esquire Article

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:38.840
that happened.
- Yeah.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.810
- Back in the 90s when Mr. Rogers--

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:42.223
- Your character was a
real writer for Esquire.

00:02:42.223 --> 00:02:43.400
- He was, he was.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:44.830
And there's this incredible article

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:48.110
that Tom Junod, the journalist
that Lloyd is based on,

00:02:48.110 --> 00:02:49.910
wrote this piece.

00:02:49.910 --> 00:02:53.880
It's very moving how he touches
on that very same subject of

00:02:53.880 --> 00:02:56.950
something that Fred Rogers
knew intrinsically well,

00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:00.380
how children relate to
these kind of talismans

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:01.800
early in your life.
- Yeah.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:03.680
So did you have one, did you have a toy

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:04.610
when you were a kid?
- I did!

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:06.570
I did, I had a teddy bear that I was given

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:10.112
the day I was born that I
very originally named Ted.

00:03:10.112 --> 00:03:12.160
(audience laughing)
- Oh, he's the O.G. Ted!

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:14.360
- The O.G. Ted.
- Is he foul mouthed?

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.080
- No, no.
(laughing)

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:17.600
Very silent, actually, doesn't say much.

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:19.740
Not much of a talker but a good listener.

00:03:19.740 --> 00:03:21.640
- I love that you have the original Ted.

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:23.870
If you've seen the movie Ted, it's, well,

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.640
it's different
(laughing)

00:03:25.640 --> 00:03:27.250
than maybe what your Ted was like.

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:30.893
- Yes, my Ted was a little
offended by that Ted.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:34.060
- So wait, I hear that Tom Hanks

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:37.011
gave you an interesting
gift at the end of the film.

00:03:37.011 --> 00:03:38.120
(laughing)

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:40.648
'Cause I am so excited about this.

00:03:40.648 --> 00:03:42.270
- Oh no, I feel terrible.

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:44.827
- Don't worry, all of you
have said the same thing.

00:03:44.827 --> 00:03:46.530
- Oh, no, that makes this worse!

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:48.040
- No!
- He's probably gonna say,

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.530
oh, I've been working
with a group of dimwits.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.770
- Tell them, so he gets this,
they all get this gift right?

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:54.520
A bunch of you got, the actors, right?

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:58.040
- Yes, a great number of us cast and crew

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:00.163
got this beautiful gift.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:04.870
It's clearly incredibly
well made, made of leather,

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:05.853
it's inscribed.

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:09.730
We're just not quite sure what it is.

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:11.600
(laughing)

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:13.220
Or maybe what to do with it.

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:14.330
- I cannot wait to ask!

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:18.222
- A journal from Mr. Hanks,
the title of my autobiography.

00:04:18.222 --> 00:04:19.055
(laughing)

